The archive was checked against the original root Cargo.lock registry checksum.
9.0.0 was the newest published version when vendored and upstream
main still used the faulty original-coordinate chunk baseline.

Local change: src/concat_sourcemap_builder.rs retains the last mapped original
line/column independently of the last generated token. An unmapped segment
does not update the original-coordinate state in VLQ encoding. That state
must survive empty and entirely unmapped chunks, for borrowed and owned maps.
The adjacent unit regression verifies serialized round-trip tokens and source
metadata for those cases.

Local change 2: src/encode.rs (estimate_mappings_length) counts the destination
lines each TokenChunk advances (tokens[t.end - 1].get_dst_line().saturating_sub(t.prev_dst_line))
instead of adding t.prev_dst_line (#109). Each chunk writes one semicolon per
destination line it advances; sparse unminified output can advance more lines
than tokens. Covered by encode_estimates_line_breaks_of_token_chunks.

Local change 3: src/encode.rs pre-allocates total_string_bytes + (total_string_bytes >> 3) + 64
(~1.125x headroom) instead of 6 * total_string_bytes worst-case escaping,
avoiding 500+ MB over-allocations on large sourcemaps, and removes the
debug_assert!(contents.len() <= max_segments) tied to the 6x bound (#553). When
tokens.len() >= 50_000 and token_chunks.len() >= 8, encode_to_string_with_null_contents
spawns up to four std::thread::scope workers for sourcesContent JSON escaping
(when at least 64 entries exist) and up to four workers for TokenChunk VLQ
mapping serialization concurrently in the same scope (up to eight worker threads
total).

Local change 4: src/sourcemap.rs adds SourceMap::redact_source_contents (filtering
source_contents entries to None in place without cloning kept strings) and
SourceMap::to_json_string_with_null_contents (calling encode_to_string_with_null_contents
in src/encode.rs) so a sourcemap whose source_contents entries were all redacted
to None still emits "sourcesContent":[null,...] instead of omitting the field (#553).

